From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d2d1: Tessellate, meshes, FillMesh, FillOpacityMask, ID2D1DeviceContext4 text

Several drawing calls of Direct2D drew nothing or returned E_NOTIMPL:
 - ID2D1Geometry::Tessellate of every geometry type was E_NOTIMPL. The geometry is
   flattened, joined with itself (so overlaps are resolved by the fill mode), triangulated
   as a path, and the triangles are handed to the sink (which the caller closes).
 - ID2D1Mesh::Open was E_NOTIMPL: it gives a tessellation sink that collects triangles
   (the mesh can be opened once, D2DERR_WRONG_STATE after that).
 - FillMesh drew nothing outside command lists: it now draws the triangles with the brush.
 - FillOpacityMask (both the render target and the device context method) drew nothing
   outside command lists: it fills the destination rectangle with the brush, with the
   alpha of the mask bitmap, set on the destination rectangle from the source rectangle, as
   the opacity.
 - ID2D1DeviceContext4::DrawText and DrawTextLayout did nothing: they draw the text as
   the render target methods do (colour fonts when asked for); the palette index and the
   SVG glyph style are ignored.
---
